class.description:
Reached through [member NetwEntity.simulation]. Each peer runs the entity in one [member mode], which decides whether [member network_process] runs and whether the body is frozen. A game sets the members below and reads [member mode].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _init() -> void:
    var entity := Netw.configure_entity(self)
    entity.simulation.bodies = [^"Sphere"]
    entity.simulation.remote_mode = NetwSimulation.REMOTE_MODE_ACTIVE

func _network_process(delta: float, tick: int, is_fresh: bool) -> void:
    if is_fresh:
        steer(delta)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public Car()
{
    var entity = Netw.ConfigureEntity(this);
    entity.Simulation.Bodies = new Godot.Collections.Array { new NodePath("Sphere") };
    entity.Simulation.RemoteMode = NetwSimulation.RemoteModeEnum.Active;
    entity.Simulation.NetworkProcess = Callable.From<double, long, bool>(NetworkProcess);
}

private void NetworkProcess(double delta, long tick, bool isFresh)
{
    if (isFresh)
        Steer(delta);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
An entity is simulated once it sets or calls anything here, is predicted as [NetwPrediction] describes, or has a [RigidBody2D] or [RigidBody3D] root drawn by [member NetwEntity.display]. Other entities stay [constant MODE_NONE].
[b]Modes[/b]
The peer writing replicated state runs [constant MODE_AUTHORITY]. A predicting client runs [constant MODE_PREDICT]. Every other copy is [constant MODE_PROXY] or [constant MODE_ACTIVE], as [member remote_mode] says.
